IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 3843 of 2020
CITATION: (2021) 11 SCC 344
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, Indu Malhotra, Indira Banerjee

PARTIES:
State of Uttarakhand vs Smt. Suman

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Maternity Benefit Act, 1961, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 5 Maternity Benefit Act, Article 42

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
maternity leave entitlement, contractual employees, gender justice, second child maternity

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that contractual female employees are entitled to full maternity benefits on equal footing with regular staff, in accordance with social justice under Article 42.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 5 Maternity Benefit Act, Article 42.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

